sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Discover accounts without releasing secrets
    accDescr: The worker derives the active top-level document and checks desktop status before discovery. NativeHost validates protocol v3 and relays over a verified Windows pipe. Integration opt-in, an explicitly unlocked vault, origin policy and quotas gate metadata. The worker validates the response and rechecks its target before showing accounts.
    participant W as Browser worker
    participant H as NativeHost
    participant A as Desktop flow
    participant C as Core vault
    W->>W: Read active tab, document ID and URL
    W->>H: Native Messaging: getStatus
    H->>A: Verified named pipe: getStatus
    A-->>H: integrationEnabled, unlocked
    H-->>W: Validated protocol v3 response
    alt Desktop closed
        W->>W: Show unavailable state
        opt User clicks Open YourSafe
            W->>H: showApp
            H->>A: Start installed YourSafe and verify pipe peer
        end
    else Disabled or locked
        W->>W: Show enable or unlock guidance
        Note over W,A: Open YourSafe restores or foregrounds the running app
    else Enabled and explicitly unlocked
        W->>H: findCredentials(canonical origin)
        H->>A: Validate frame and forward one request
        A->>A: Check opt-in, normal unlock and quota
        A->>C: Serialized GetAutofillCredentials
        C-->>A: Active password or TOTP account metadata
        A->>A: Match saved URL origin exactly
        A-->>H: Bounded IDs, titles, usernames, flags
        H-->>W: credentials and truncated flag
        W->>W: Validate schema and recheck same target
        W->>W: Show accounts for explicit selection
    end
    Note over W,C: Discovery returns no password, TOTP seed or recovery codes
